From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:23:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] test: pin macos_os_tests_gate.gh_api's gh timeout
 (hung gh fails open)

Mutant M11 (gh_api `subprocess.run(..., timeout=60)` -> no timeout) survived
every test in tests/ci/test_macos_os_tests_workflow.py: the fail-open tests
inject TimeoutExpired through a fake `api`, so nothing pinned that the real
gh_api bounds the call. Without the timeout a hung `gh api` holds the Linux
gate job until its timeout-minutes: 10, the gate job fails and the scheduled
test job is skipped (a red run instead of fail-open to testing).

The new test swaps the gate module's own `subprocess` name (not the global
module) for a namespace whose run() records the timeout kwarg and raises
TimeoutExpired, then runs decide("schedule", gate.gh_api, ...). It asserts the
run goes ahead ("running anyway") and every recorded timeout is a number in
(0, 120], well under the gate job's 10-minute cap.

Proof: sdlc-review scripts/mutants.py, anchor `, timeout=60)` -> `)` in
scripts/ci/macos_os_tests_gate.py: baseline 17 passed; mutant killed, failing
only test_a_hung_gh_read_is_bounded_and_fails_open_to_testing. Whole file
17 passed, 0 skipped. Test-only change.

Found by post-merge check t_01a1d6de440800cd (core PR #2655). Card
t_01a1d6fe45c0ccfe.
---
 tests/ci/test_macos_os_tests_workflow.py | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/ci/test_macos_os_tests_workflow.py b/tests/ci/test_macos_os_tests_workflow.py
index ef63862230..b9d03c1ffb 100644
--- a/tests/ci/test_macos_os_tests_workflow.py
+++ b/tests/ci/test_macos_os_tests_workflow.py
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@ from __future__ import annotations
 
 import importlib.util
 import subprocess
+import types
 from pathlib import Path
 
 import hermes_yaml
@@ -159,6 +160,28 @@ def test_unreadable_queue_fails_open_to_testing(error):
     assert "running anyway" in reason
 
 
+def test_a_hung_gh_read_is_bounded_and_fails_open_to_testing(monkeypatch):
+    # The real gh_api must bound each `gh api` call: without a timeout a hung read holds the
+    # gate job until its 10-minute cap, the gate fails and the scheduled test job is skipped.
+    gate = _gate()
+    timeouts: list[object] = []
+
+    def run(argv, **kwargs):
+        timeouts.append(kwargs.get("timeout"))
+        raise subprocess.TimeoutExpired(argv, kwargs.get("timeout") or 0)
+
+    # Patch the gate module's own subprocess name, not the global module.
+    fake = types.SimpleNamespace(run=run, SubprocessError=subprocess.SubprocessError,
+                                 TimeoutExpired=subprocess.TimeoutExpired,
+                                 CalledProcessError=subprocess.CalledProcessError)
+    monkeypatch.setattr(gate, "subprocess", fake)
+    run_it, reason = gate.decide("schedule", gate.gh_api, REPO, own_run_id=1)
+    assert run_it is True
+    assert "running anyway" in reason
+    assert timeouts, "gh_api never called subprocess.run"
+    assert all(isinstance(t, (int, float)) and 0 < t <= 120 for t in timeouts), timeouts
+
+
 def test_main_writes_the_step_output(tmp_path, monkeypatch):
     gate = _gate()
     out = tmp_path / "out"
